From: junsulee <junsulee119@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: cedrus: size the low-2-bit plane from the stride the engine uses

Not part of the LibreELEC series. Found by stockmind (handtop issue #8).

For 10-bit output the engine writes a low-2-bit plane after the 8-bit
reconstruction. The capture buffer reserved ALIGN(width / 4, 32) bytes per
row for it, but VP9 programs the plane stride as ALIGN(bytesperline / 4, 32)
of the reconstruction surface: the 64-byte aligned capture stride (0002), or
ALIGN(width, 16) for the hidden surface behind P010. At widths 128k + 1 to
128k + 3 (1281, 1409, ...) that is 32 bytes more per row, so the engine
writes up to 32 * 1.5 * height bytes (about 35 KB at 720 lines) past the end
of the buffer. Without an IOMMU that is DMA into whatever lies next in CMA,
and any 10-bit VP9 stream with such a width reaches it.

Size the plane from the reconstruction stride instead. H.265 programs
ALIGN(width / 4, 32), which is never larger, so it is covered as well. The
cost is at most 32 * 1.5 * height bytes of extra buffer at those widths and
nothing at the others (bytesperline / 4 rounds to the same 32 bytes).

LibreELEC 0438 fixes the same allocation as part of a larger layout rework
(issue #8); drop this patch when 0438 is taken.
---
--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus.h
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus.h
@@ -262,10 +262,17 @@
 /*
  * Size of the low-2-bit plane the hardware appends after the 8-bit NV12
  * planes for 10-bit reconstruction.  Shared by all codecs.
+ *
+ * Sized from the stride of the reconstruction surface, not from the picture
+ * width: VP9 programs the plane stride as ALIGN(bytesperline / 4, 32), and
+ * bytesperline is the 64-byte aligned capture stride (16 for the hidden P010
+ * surface).  ALIGN(width / 4, 32) is smaller for widths 128k + 1 to 128k + 3
+ * (1281, for example), and the engine then writes 32 bytes per row past the
+ * end of the buffer.  H.265 uses ALIGN(width / 4, 32), which this covers.
  */
-static inline u32 cedrus_dst_2bit_size(unsigned int width, unsigned int height)
+static inline u32 cedrus_dst_2bit_size(unsigned int stride, unsigned int height)
 {
-	return ALIGN(width / 4, 32) * height * 3 / 2;
+	return ALIGN(stride / 4, 32) * height * 3 / 2;
 }
 
 static inline bool cedrus_dst_is_p010(struct cedrus_ctx *ctx)
@@ -334,10 +341,12 @@
 	if (ctx->bit_depth <= 8)
 		return 0;
 
-	extra = cedrus_dst_2bit_size(pix_fmt->width, pix_fmt->height);
-
 	if (pix_fmt->pixelformat == V4L2_PIX_FMT_P010)
-		extra += ALIGN(pix_fmt->width, 16) * pix_fmt->height * 3 / 2;
+		/* hidden NV12 surface, see cedrus_dst_frame_fmt() */
+		extra = cedrus_dst_2bit_size(ALIGN(pix_fmt->width, 16), pix_fmt->height) +
+			ALIGN(pix_fmt->width, 16) * pix_fmt->height * 3 / 2;
+	else
+		extra = cedrus_dst_2bit_size(pix_fmt->bytesperline, pix_fmt->height);
 
 	return extra;
 }
